    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="namespaceGambit_1_1ColliderBit_1_1ATLAS" kindref="compound">ATLAS</ref> ZH(-&gt;photon+gravitino) (79.8 fb^-1) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Based on:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ulink url="https://atlas.web.cern.ch/Atlas/GROUPS/PHYSICS/CONFNOTES/ATLAS-CONF-2018-019/">https://atlas.web.cern.ch/Atlas/GROUPS/PHYSICS/CONFNOTES/ATLAS-CONF-2018-019/</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ulink url="https://cds.cern.ch/record/2621481/files/ATLAS-CONF-2018-019.pdf">https://cds.cern.ch/record/2621481/files/ATLAS-CONF-2018-019.pdf</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Andy Buckley</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Conservative underestimate of yield in benchmark point cutflow 5.2 vs 8.7 passing all cuts: underestimation of MET and satisfaction of angular/balance cuts. Adding MET smearing doesn&apos;t appear to have helped. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
